{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>When you take</b> It is juxtaposed to כי תשא — a hint to what they said: their horn was raised in כי תשא. And יוה\"כ is juxtaposed to כופר נפשו to say that on יום הכפורים one must give כופר נפשו, for then all the people are counted and pass before Him, and therefore the custom is to pledge charity on יום הכפורים. תשא את ראש בני — rashei tevot, equals the numerical value of תר\"ג, for thus were the thousands: ת\"ר אלף and ג' אלפים, and likewise בנ\"י equals תר\"ג." "<b>And they shall give</b> If you read it in reverse, it likewise becomes ונתנו — לך: all that a person gives to charity returns to him and he lacks nothing on its account. ג\"פ פקודים and ג\"פ מחצית השקל in the parashah, and ג\"פ כופר נפשו, and ג\"פ לכפר, and ג\"פ בנ\"י — to atone for three things: for war, famine, and pestilence. And likewise Gad the seer said to David when he counted Israel: three I am bringing upon you."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:47.652125364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}